WEBVTT

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:28.300
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:28.300
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:28.300
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:53.880 --> 00:02:02.300
The 3rd Battle of Tiamat

00:01:53.880 --> 00:02:02.300
Part II

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:09.650
In February of Space Year 795,
Imperial Year 486...

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:16.150
...the 330th battle between the Free
Planets Alliance and Imperial fleets...

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:19.900
...was taking place in Tiamat Starzone.

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:25.590
But Reinhard's fleet, which was ordered to the rear as a reserve had not yet participated in the battle.

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:31.240
All ships, withdraw.

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:39.100
Admiral, what are you thinking, retreating 
without orders from General Headquarters...

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:42.730
...and without exchanging fire 
with the enemy even once ?

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:44.700
Don't make me repeat myself.

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:48.850
If we advance now, it'll only 
further contribute to the chaos.

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:52.190
Instead, we should retreat to maintain space for our side to retreat also...

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:57.100
...then we can lure the enemy fleet further in
and lead them to exceed the point of no return.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:58.820
That's the important thing to do.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.920
But there has been no orders from General Headquarters...

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:03.450
If we were not allowed to do anything without orders from General HQ...

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:06.320
...then there would be no
need for fleet commanders.

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:10.020
In each individual situation, we act
based on the commander's judgement.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:10.860
But...

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:12.690
The same goes for the 
Chief Staff Officer as well.

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:15.500
If we only needed to blindly follow General HQ orders...

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:19.240
...the Fleet CSO would be
the least necessary officer.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:20.240
Don't you agree ?!

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:31.190
A portion of the enemy fleet is retreating without fighting.

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:32.550
This is our chance.

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:35.150
We'll annihilate the enemy in
one breath by taking advantage of it.

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:35.660
Go !

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:36.800
Our victory is right before us !

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.300
Admiral, the 11th Fleet is 
advancing further forward.

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:53.370
Are you okay with this ?

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:55.800
It looks like a trap to me.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:58.180
It's difficult to tell.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:03:59.300
Really ?

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:02.670
Everything is a matter of viewpoint.

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:05.850
Holland's actions are
undoubtedly reckless...

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:10.250
...but if his opponent is weaker, 
victory will belong to the Alliance.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.250
But I wonder...

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:13.800
There's an incoming transmission
from the 10th Fleet.

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:18.250
Admiral Bucock...

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:22.180
...I'd like to request your cooperation in restraining Holland's reckless behavior.

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:25.200
He may know how
to ignore old tactics...

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:28.790
...but I don't think he's capable of constructing a new set of tactics.

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:34.550
But, Admiral Ulanfu, he seems to be on a roll and winning so far.

00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:38.240
Perhaps we might win
it in a called{suspended ?} game.

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:42.100
I can hope that the thing 
called "so far" continues...

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:44.510
...but the limit is inching
closer and closer.

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:48.650
If the Imperial fleet has even one
commander with any foresight...

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:53.300
...he'll withdraw from the midst of this chaos and wait for an opportunity to counterattack.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:55.850
In this instance, even
if we incur his displeasure...

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:59.600
...we should restrain him and bring him back,
or else we might go down with him.

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:03.530
Admiral Bucock, have you
heard what he's been saying ?

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:09.400
Holland calls himself the revival of Admiral Bruce Ashbey.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:15.160
When he became a Vice Admiral,
he was 32 years old, just like Ashbey.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:19.640
If he becomes a Fleet Admiral before the age of 35, he'll surpass Ashbey.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:25.000
But as you say, there seems to be a man of foresight within the Imperial fleet.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:28.360
One portion of the fleet
is retreating without fighting.

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:31.740
It does look like a withdrawal, not desertion or confusion.

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:34.550
I see, you noticed it, too.

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:36.480
Of course I did.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:39.790
The only person who wouldn't notice it would be that empty-headed Holland.

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:44.220
Advancement and victory, withdrawal
and defeat - he can't even tell them apart.

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:47.720
Such foolish fleet 
movements can't continue forever.

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:50.660
The time it's taking for him to reach the point of no-return is only decreasing.

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:53.950
If that commander possesses
sufficient combat potential...

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:58.740
...he'll drag Holland into the center
of a circle and beat him senseless.

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:00.390
Doesn't he{i.e. Holland} even realize this ?

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:06.660
I would think that to retreat when one is
winning - or when one thinks one is winning...

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:11.450
...would be more difficult than walking
away when one gets dumped by a woman.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:15.000
Don't you think, Admiral Ulanfu ?

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:19.130
I see, you're right.

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:20.550
As far as we're concerned...

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:27.300
...we can only prepare to prevent disaster to the entire fleet when the 11th gets routed.

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:34.310
But it's cruel to allow the servicemen of the 
11th Fleet to suffer as meaningless sacrifices.

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:36.870
We can't just sit back and do nothing.

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:40.500
I will continue to send 
withdrawal orders to Holland.

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:54.510
The enemy is approaching us !

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:56.200
I can see that.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:00.300
Aren't you going to
intercept them, Commander ?

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:05.540
Sir, should we move the fleet-line slightly forward and return fire ?

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:12.650
Oh, I see.
That's what he means.

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:16.200
No, it's still early.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:18.590
We'll withdraw further.

00:07:18.590 --> 00:07:21.590
Lt. Commander Kircheis, 
we don't need to be impatient.

00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:24.420
In a short while, the enemy will reach the point of no-return.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:27.090
That will be the moment 
we launch our counterattack.

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:28.510
Remember that.

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:30.100
Yes, Admiral.

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:31.590
I apologize for my presumption.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:40.900
He's not even listening ?

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:43.600
Even though Kircheis
was being so considerate ?

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:53.290
This is why he shouldn't
be nice to everyone.

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:10.430
Between 16:40 and 19:20, the situation was proceeding favorably for the Alliance fleet.

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:12.470
Take that !

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:15.230
My fleet is the only one fighting.

00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:17.470
The achievements will be all mine.

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:21.480
With just one fleet, I'm toying with an 
enemy almost four times larger than us.

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:24.810
Even Ashbey couldn't have 
engineered such a beautiful victory !

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:29.660
Yeah, even Limpao and Bruce 
Ashbey were merely on defense.

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:31.080
I'm different !

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:36.600
I will annihilate the enemy, thrust past
Iserlohn Fortress, then march to attack Odin.

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:40.720
I will execute the Emperor
and destroy the Empire.

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:46.090
"Fleet Admiral Willem Holland, the one who destroyed the Empire" - that will be me !

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:49.810
Admiral, there's an incoming
transmission from the 5th Fleet.

00:08:51.190 --> 00:08:52.500
"We've garnered enough
fruits from this battle."

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:54.780
"Avoid taking your pursuit
too deep, and retreat."

00:08:54.780 --> 00:08:55.480
That's all.

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:56.360
Bullshit !

00:08:56.360 --> 00:09:00.950
That old man is envious because my victory is so brilliant.

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:03.510
It's a response from the 11th Fleet.

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:05.450
"The signs of enemy ships
in front of us are few."

00:09:05.450 --> 00:09:09.070
"We will continue to advance,
divide them up, and annihilate them."

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:09.900
That's all.

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:11.020
Admiral.

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:12.720
Send a message again.

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:15.150
"Before inviting the enemy's
all-out counterattack..."

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:17.280
"...we should retreat while 
we have the upper hand..."

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:20.620
"...and restore order among all fleets."

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:21.380
Yes, sir.

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:25.900
Send them a response.

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:28.240
"A pioneer is always unrecognized."

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:29.700
"As of now, further discussion ..."

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:31.580
"...and non-cooperative
attitudes must cease."

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:34.950
"Right now, I will move forward,
in search of eternal achievement..."

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:36.920
"...and will only seek my 
supporters in the future."

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:40.560
I see.

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:43.970
Pioneers are always called insane.

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:47.840
But being insane doesn't
always make you a pioneer.

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:49.930
Send him another
withdrawal directive.

00:09:49.930 --> 00:09:55.210
Tell him that if he doesn't retreat, we'll accuse him of glory-seeking at his court martial.

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:57.710
I don't care !

00:09:57.710 --> 00:10:00.780
I made the plans for this
battle to begin with !

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:04.840
That's why Fleet Admiral Lobos left me
in charge of executing this battle plan !

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:07.330
And just who exactly 
created this present victory ?

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:11.200
At the court, I'll show
them who is righteous !

00:10:12.700 --> 00:10:13.600
Admiral...

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:15.650
Cut off any further communications.

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:17.500
It's just a damn nuisance.

00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:23.350
Holland advanced his
fleet even further...

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:27.850
...running wild through the Imperial fleet with pioneer-like tactics.

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:32.110
Against this, the disastrous state of the Imperial fleet was rather disgraceful.

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:38.300
What on earth are they doing ?

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:41.940
Why do they have to go along with the rebel fleet's disorderly movements ?

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:46.450
If they want to dance, we should just let them dance on a stage spotlighted by darkness.

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:48.950
Why is there a need for
us to extend ourselves...

00:10:48.950 --> 00:10:51.340
...follow their steps and tangle our legs in the process ?

00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:05.500
They're all idiots.

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:08.950
Of course, that's how we
get promoted so fast.

00:11:08.950 --> 00:11:10.950
But then again, unless we
find some useful people...

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:13.650
...it'll create an obstacle to the realization of our ambitions.

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:18.200
It's not like the two of us can do each
and every thing that needs to be done.

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:23.480
This battle also seems meaningless in terms of talent hunting.

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:25.130
It'll be over soon, won't it ?

00:11:25.130 --> 00:11:26.000
That's right.

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:29.250
They'll reach their limits
before my patience does.

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:34.050
Lord Reinhard, the threshold of your
patience seems to have grown very high.

00:11:34.050 --> 00:11:35.180
Of course it has.

00:11:35.180 --> 00:11:38.230
I've been training ever since military preparatory school.

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:40.100
I wonder how many times
I've restrained myself...

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:43.550
...from killing those bastards who probably should have been killed.

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:53.050
It's almost time.

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:59.450
Commander, it seems the outcome of the battle has been determined.

00:11:59.450 --> 00:12:02.000
We should retreat 
before we suffer any losses.

00:12:03.590 --> 00:12:06.410
The enemy attack is nearing its end.

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:08.370
There's no such thing
as perpetual motion.

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:13.290
If we concentrate our attack on the enemy
nucleus at a point where their activities end...

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:15.950
...their sand-castle victory
will crumble quickly.

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:17.500
So why should we retreat now ?

00:12:17.980 --> 00:12:19.590
That's just armchair theory.

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:21.800
Don't be hung up on that
and please just withdraw.

00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:24.920
What the hell has he
been listening to up to now ?

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:27.290
Shut up, you coward !

00:12:27.290 --> 00:12:30.750
It's impudent of you to speak of losing in the first place...

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:34.640
...and then you dare to interfere with a commander's authority ?

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:41.680
All ships under my command,
prepare to launch an artillery attack.

00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:43.750
When the order is given, fire.

00:12:44.350 --> 00:12:45.800
All ships, prepare to
launch an artillery attack.

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:49.200
At that moment, the 11th Fleet...

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:53.470
...which had been pounding on its enemy with a storm-like power, just stopped.

00:12:53.470 --> 00:12:57.550
Having reached the limit of their activities the fleet was transitioning from expansion to cessation...

00:12:57.550 --> 00:12:59.940
...and their movements
momentarily froze.

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:02.550
And at the very moment that its 
congealment was about to thaw...

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:04.140
All ships, fire your main cannons !

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:13.110
Direct hit coming !

00:13:27.100 --> 00:13:29.450
Prepare for a second artillery attack.

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:29.950
Fire !

00:13:31.110 --> 00:13:33.040
It was the finishing blow.

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:38.680
Having lost its commander, the 11th Fleet
was nothing more than a disorderly crowd.

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:41.950
Though Holland dominated
the battlefield for four hours...

00:13:41.950 --> 00:13:46.360
...Reinhard simply executed two artillery attacks in 3 minutes.

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:50.650
Regardless, the decisive
victory belonged to Reinhard.

00:13:50.650 --> 00:13:53.740
It was unnecessary to dominate the battleground from the beginning.

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:56.770
Look !

00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:02.450
We shouldn't pursue
a follow-up attack ?

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:04.410
Kircheis, why ?

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:11.450
You shouldn't have to bother 
with chasing after fleeing troops.

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:13.400
That's all.

00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:15.460
We've accomplished enough already.

00:14:15.460 --> 00:14:19.200
The commendation for hunting down stragglers can be shared among the other admirals.

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:21.100
That's what he means.

00:14:21.100 --> 00:14:24.550
I see, that's all there is to it.

00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:30.810
Then let us just watch
our side's winning battle.

00:14:40.300 --> 00:14:43.550
As I thought, he will not be
of any use to Lord Reinhard.

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:50.950
Though the other Imperial fleets zealously pursued the remains of the 11th Fleet...

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:55.510
...the Alliance 5th and 10th Fleets, having
prepared for this situation, got in their way.

00:14:57.530 --> 00:14:58.160
Fire !

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:03.450
Fire !

00:15:06.150 --> 00:15:10.260
The formation of the Imperial fleet was broken apart, and its movement froze momentarily...

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:14.240
...but soon they resumed their advance and continued to pursue the Alliance fleet.

00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:18.950
Bucock and Ulanfu made 
well-coordinated movements and retreated...

00:15:18.950 --> 00:15:22.540
...covering for the remaining
ships of the 11th Fleet.

00:15:23.090 --> 00:15:25.500
Several attempts by
the Imperial fleet to attack...

00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:29.350
...were thwarted by the flexible and indestructible defense line...

00:15:29.350 --> 00:15:31.400
...and the Imperial fleet finally
had to give up on the pursuit...

00:15:31.400 --> 00:15:33.940
...without dealing a fatal
blow to the Alliance fleet.

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:41.000
There is some talent over
in the Alliance forces.

00:15:42.020 --> 00:15:44.350
Shall we send a message
commending them for their effort ?

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:48.880
Let's not do that at this point.

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:53.860
At the Second Battle of Tiamat, Vice Admiral Steiermark sent a condolence message...

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:56.500
...on the death of the enemy commander Bruce Ashbey...

00:15:56.500 --> 00:15:59.860
...but he incurred the brass's
antagonism for that act.

00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:02.290
I'm still just a mere Vice Admiral.

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:08.510
After I gain command of all troops and no one can complain about what I do, I'll do that{i.e. sending a telegram}.

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:16.940
The Alliance fleet regrouped
and returned to their home planet.

00:16:16.940 --> 00:16:19.940
What remained of the 11th Fleet was a complete wreck...

00:16:19.940 --> 00:16:22.110
...and it would take a lot
of work to rebuild it.

00:16:23.100 --> 00:16:26.200
Because of his death in the battle, Holland evaded punishment.

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:27.950
In another situation, he'd have been
granted a special double promotion...

00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:31.680
...for his death and become a Fleet Admiral
but his punishment would most likely prevent it.

00:16:33.490 --> 00:16:36.750
Though Bucock and Ulanfu 
prevented a disaster to all the fleets...

00:16:36.750 --> 00:16:39.950
...they still regretted their inability to restrain Holland's reckless actions.

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:44.380
It seems Willem Holland
failed to become a hero.

00:16:44.380 --> 00:16:45.640
A "hero" huh ?

00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:48.880
Admiral Ulanfu, did you know ?

00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:53.170
There was someone who said 
something interesting about being a "hero."

00:16:53.170 --> 00:16:53.860
Oh ?

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:56.860
"Heroes abound at a bar table."

00:16:56.860 --> 00:17:00.430
"But you can't find a hero in the
surgery chair in the dentist's office."

00:17:00.430 --> 00:17:03.450
Essentially, a "hero" is just like that.

00:17:04.650 --> 00:17:08.240
I see, there seems to
be no disagreement there.

00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:10.750
Who might that shrewd critic be ?

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:16.600
I heard he was one of Admiral Sitolet student's when he was still headmaster of the military academy.

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:19.670
What was his name again...?

00:17:19.670 --> 00:17:22.950
It was a simple name - 
an Asian name, similar to yours.

00:17:22.950 --> 00:17:25.750
I've heard it a few times, but...

00:17:25.750 --> 00:17:27.200
Admiral...

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:29.300
...a friendly fleet is in front of us.

00:17:29.300 --> 00:17:31.200
Oh, they finally came.

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:34.750
Bogged down by the weight of responsibility for taking the fleet back from the defeat...

00:17:34.750 --> 00:17:37.980
...Bucock couldn't remember.

00:17:37.980 --> 00:17:42.300
It was after he arrived at Heinessen that he recalled the name, "Yang."

00:17:44.300 --> 00:17:47.300
Since the Alliance forces sent in a reinforcement fleet...

00:17:47.300 --> 00:17:50.440
...the Imperial fleet retreated
from the Tiamat Starzone.

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:56.740
With their victory in battle there was no need to continue occupying an inhabited starzone.

00:17:56.740 --> 00:18:01.000
From the beginning, the battle had had no meaning other than for domestic publicity.

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:04.130
That objective was more
than sufficiently fulfilled.

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:12.070
Reinhard made a name for himself by changing the momentum of the battle with just one artillery attack.

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:19.100
Many thought that he was just lucky, but he was still assessed to have rendered distinguished service.

00:18:19.100 --> 00:18:21.870
With this, his promotion to full Admiral was all but decided.

00:18:23.630 --> 00:18:28.350
For the time being, Fate seems to have sold you her favors.

00:18:28.350 --> 00:18:29.760
Fate ?

00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:33.240
I don't plan on letting
Fate control my life.

00:18:33.240 --> 00:18:39.000
By my strength, I will rise, and
because of my shortcomings, I will fall.

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:41.850
Everything will be determined by the extent of my talent.

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:47.800
And if you and I cooperate, we can go
on without having Fate interfere with us.

00:18:47.800 --> 00:18:49.020
That's admirable.

00:18:49.570 --> 00:18:51.050
At least that's what I try to do.

00:18:57.670 --> 00:19:00.800
After his return, Reinhard 
was promoted to full Admiral.

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:05.290
Except for the Goldenbaum
family's male children...

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:10.160
...obtaining the rank of Admiral at age 19
was unheard of in the history of the Empire.

00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:13.970
Kircheis was promoted
to Commander as well.

00:19:13.970 --> 00:19:19.700
Since his duty remained being an aide to Reinhard, he felt relieved.

00:19:20.610 --> 00:19:24.850
Though Reinhard was promoted, his duty was undetermined...

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:27.960
...and he was just given the temporary titles of High Secretary in the Ministry of the Military...

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:32.870
...and Member of a Permanent Committee in the Space Fleet Supreme Staff Office.

00:19:34.240 --> 00:19:36.300
Both are honorary positions...

00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:40.500
...and it was evident that though they
were willing to give him status and honor...

00:19:40.500 --> 00:19:42.870
...the military brass didn't intend to give him any actual authority.

00:19:44.360 --> 00:19:45.350
Despite that...

00:19:45.350 --> 00:19:49.400
...there was a reward for the Admiral that
Reinhard was wholeheartedly pleased with.

00:19:49.400 --> 00:19:51.400
He was given a personal flagship.

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:54.090
It's this way.

00:19:54.090 --> 00:19:56.400
Of course, it is still the
property of the government...

00:19:56.400 --> 00:19:59.100
...but it cannot be taken away
without the consent of the user.

00:20:00.090 --> 00:20:02.750
Unless the user requests a replacement...

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:09.430
...retires from service, is demoted, or dies in battle, it was Reinhard's possession.

00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:25.570
This is the newly 
built warship, Brunhilde...

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:29.650
It's an experimental manufacture for the next generation warship...

00:20:29.650 --> 00:20:32.250
...featuring an armor system
based on new theories.

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:37.160
It's slightly smaller than conventional
flagships, but its firepower is superior.

00:20:38.950 --> 00:20:40.550
Because it's an experimental ship...

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:43.800
...it's laden with equipment that ignores mass production costs.

00:20:47.570 --> 00:20:50.750
I cannot thank you enough for 
providing me with such a splendid ship.

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:52.600
Please convey this 
message to His Majesty.

00:20:56.260 --> 00:20:58.370
Well then, please feel
free to take a look.

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:03.900
Brunhilde...Brunhilde...

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:05.400
It really is an amazing ship.

00:21:06.470 --> 00:21:08.580
This ship is half yours.

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:12.000
Since you're a Commander, you are qualified
to be captain of this ship, but do you want to ?

00:21:13.690 --> 00:21:15.450
That sounds nice...

00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:22.950
...as long as you give me permission to direct my loyalty to Brunhilde above all, that is.

00:21:22.950 --> 00:21:24.330
That's troublesome.

00:21:24.330 --> 00:21:25.660
I retract my previous statement.

00:21:25.660 --> 00:21:27.900
I'll appoint someone else as captain.

00:21:28.570 --> 00:21:30.410
I think that would be better.

00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:36.350
Anyway, you're thinking you want to take this
ship into battle as soon as possible, aren't you ?

00:21:36.350 --> 00:21:39.330
Unfortunately, there probably 
won't be any battles for a while.

00:21:39.330 --> 00:21:41.550
I wish some regional
revolt would break out...

00:21:41.550 --> 00:21:44.090
...something that's
conveniently sized for quelling.

00:21:44.090 --> 00:21:48.400
If it's just conveniently sized, it won't be what you need.{place.}

00:21:48.400 --> 00:21:51.810
There are many who want to claim easy battlefield achievements.

00:21:51.810 --> 00:21:53.210
I suppose.

00:21:53.210 --> 00:21:56.300
Well, I guess we have no choice but to wait till they all die.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.750
But, sooner than
Reinhard anticipated...

00:22:02.750 --> 00:22:07.570
...the opportunity for Brunhilde's first battle came only four months later.

00:22:07.570 --> 00:22:10.500
An expedition to the
Iserlohn area is carried out...

00:22:10.500 --> 00:22:18.000
...and the fourth large-scale battle in Tiamat Starzone takes place.

00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:25.590
And there, Reinhard gets acquainted for the first time with his lifetime rival, Yang Wenli.

00:22:26.490 --> 00:22:29.750
That is the beginning of this grand epic...

00:22:29.750 --> 00:22:35.020
...and is the moment when the wheel of galactic history begins to turn.{cog moves one step.}

00:22:36.570 --> 00:22:40.130
But there was no way Reinhard could have known that at this moment.

00:22:40.130 --> 00:22:46.230
Right now, he was fast climbing the stairs of ambition with his friend, just looking upward.

00:22:49.730 --> 00:22:54.710
In some ways, it may have
been a moment of happiness.

00:22:54.710 --> 00:23:01.550
And they{i.e. Reinhard and Kircheis} believed that this moment of happiness would last forever.

